<fmt-footnote-container><fmt-fn-body id="_3c61b6a3-5a74-1c4a-a6e2-3006a34b9682" target="_3407e952-23b5-5a11-744c-2a782cefa273" reference="1"><semx element="fn" source="_3407e952-23b5-5a11-744c-2a782cefa273"><p id="_4b8b82d7-3c07-909b-0978-c659513a0b04" semx-id="_4b8b82d7-3c07-909b-0978-c659513a0b04"><fmt-fn-label><span class="fmt-caption-label"><sup>1</sup></span><span class="fmt-caption-delim"><tab/></span></fmt-fn-label>ISO 19152</p>
</semx></fmt-fn-body><fmt-fn-body id="_5b7927f0-4bc0-3045-433d-4eb6b0ee6f62" target="_22785cec-16a7-d2f7-7f54-0c1a2f45bd41" reference="2"><semx element="fn" source="_22785cec-16a7-d2f7-7f54-0c1a2f45bd41"><p id="_baa76c01-6e2b-9146-9ea0-5a0be5f6e6ef" semx-id="_baa76c01-6e2b-9146-9ea0-5a0be5f6e6ef"><fmt-fn-label><span class="fmt-caption-label"><sup>2</sup></span><span class="fmt-caption-delim"><tab/></span></fmt-fn-label>PT\_Locale is defined in ISO 19139 and ISO 19115-3 which are the XML encodings for metadata, although the structure allows any text string to include an identifier of language and text in that language..</p>
</semx></fmt-fn-body><fmt-fn-body id="_1e062a8f-406b-ef1b-16fc-e8d63155a7a4" target="_522e58ba-06a4-3752-19ba-beedb62ade20" reference="3"><semx element="fn" source="_522e58ba-06a4-3752-19ba-beedb62ade20"><p id="_4cbe3c9e-9e7f-c7c1-0436-0aef4b024251" semx-id="_4cbe3c9e-9e7f-c7c1-0436-0aef4b024251"><fmt-fn-label><span class="fmt-caption-label"><sup>3</sup></span><span class="fmt-caption-delim"><tab/></span></fmt-fn-label>ISO 19152 LADM clause 4.1.13</p>
</semx></fmt-fn-body></fmt-footnote-container></metanorma>